1
00:00:00,834 --> 00:00:04,421
[theme music playing]

2
00:00:11,094 --> 00:00:14,389
<i>-We need to meet.</i>
<i>-All right. I'll be there.</i>

3
00:00:14,472 --> 00:00:18,018
[Emilia]<i> You follow that Camia woman.</i>
<i>I'll follow Ivy Aguas.</i>

4
00:00:18,101 --> 00:00:20,937
[Camia]<i> As much as I want</i>
<i>to stop worrying, Lily, I can't.</i>

5
00:00:21,020 --> 00:00:22,856
<i>Especially since you've reached</i>
<i>the point of having</i>

6
00:00:22,939 --> 00:00:24,774
<i>a relationship with the enemy.</i>

7
00:00:24,858 --> 00:00:26,818
<i>How long will this go on, Lily?</i>
<i>Until marriage?</i>

8
00:00:26,901 --> 00:00:28,194
[Ivy] <i>I won't let it get that far.</i>

9
00:00:28,278 --> 00:00:29,487
<i>You have to watch out.</i>

10
00:00:29,571 --> 00:00:31,322
<i>I'm worried that Emilia</i>
<i>might get desperate,</i>

11
00:00:31,406 --> 00:00:33,450
<i>and you don't know what she's capable of.</i>

12
00:00:33,533 --> 00:00:35,785
<i>We used to be helpless</i>
<i>against the cruel Ardientes,</i>

13
00:00:35,869 --> 00:00:38,538
<i>but now we can hold our own against them.</i>

14
00:00:38,621 --> 00:00:40,915
<i>It's from Jaguar.</i>

15
00:00:40,999 --> 00:00:45,003
<i>That money is very important</i>
<i>because we will use it for the elections.</i>

16
00:00:45,086 --> 00:00:47,088
[Arnaldo] <i>Don't worry,</i>
<i>I'll guard it with all my life.</i>

17
00:00:47,172 --> 00:00:50,133
[Emilia] <i>I have no patience</i>
<i>for Ivy, Aunt Claire.</i>

18
00:00:50,216 --> 00:00:52,552
<i>I have to resort back to my old tricks.</i>

19
00:00:52,635 --> 00:00:54,596
[Claire] <i>Like what you did to Camia Cruz?</i>

20
00:00:54,679 --> 00:00:56,639
<i>Are you ready for your new assignment?</i>

21
00:00:56,723 --> 00:00:58,600
<i>-Yes, ma'am.</i>
<i>-Good.</i>

22
00:00:58,683 --> 00:01:00,643
<i>-Ivy, I'm going to break in.</i>
-[Ivy] <i>Diego, don't.</i>

23
00:01:00,727 --> 00:01:03,396
<i>We have to make sure what's inside first.</i>

24
00:01:03,480 --> 00:01:06,441
<i>We might find some important evidence.</i>

25
00:01:06,524 --> 00:01:07,776
[Arnaldo] <i>Who were you talking to?</i>

26
00:01:07,859 --> 00:01:10,070
[Ivy] <i>You're doubting me too?</i>

27
00:01:10,153 --> 00:01:12,238
<i>I'm sorry if I upset you.</i>

28
00:01:12,322 --> 00:01:13,823
<i>I think the only way</i>

29
00:01:13,907 --> 00:01:16,618
<i>we can fix this is for you</i>
<i>to have dinner with my mom.</i>

30
00:01:16,701 --> 00:01:18,620
<i>Ivy agreed to have dinner with you.</i>

31
00:01:18,703 --> 00:01:20,455
<i>Are you excited for our dinner?</i>

32
00:01:20,538 --> 00:01:22,499
<i>-Of course.</i>
<i>-I shall see you.</i>

33
00:01:23,208 --> 00:01:25,210
[Ivy] <i>I'm very excited, Emilia.</i>

34
00:01:25,293 --> 00:01:28,046
<i>Emilia and I are having dinner</i>
<i>at the Viento.</i>

35
00:01:28,129 --> 00:01:29,047
[Diego] <i>Ivy, be careful.</i>

36
00:01:29,130 --> 00:01:32,717
[Ivy] <i>Where's Emilia?</i>
<i>I said, where is Emilia?</i>

37
00:01:32,801 --> 00:01:33,927
[grunts]

38
00:01:36,054 --> 00:01:38,515
[goon] All right! Strip her clothes!

39
00:01:38,598 --> 00:01:42,101
[goons holler]

40
00:01:45,563 --> 00:01:47,357
[goon] Take them off!

41
00:01:49,192 --> 00:01:52,946
[goons laughing, hollering]

42
00:01:56,282 --> 00:01:57,784
[goon] Strip her naked!

43
00:01:57,867 --> 00:01:59,953
[goons whooping, laughing]

44
00:02:01,746 --> 00:02:04,582
[goons laughing, speaking indistinctly]

45
00:02:07,168 --> 00:02:09,087
[goon] Strip her naked!

46
00:02:10,296 --> 00:02:13,383
[goons whooping and hollering]

47
00:02:14,509 --> 00:02:16,094
[young Lily] <i>Mister, please don't. Please.</i>

48
00:02:16,177 --> 00:02:16,928
<i>Mister!</i>

49
00:02:17,011 --> 00:02:20,765
<i>Please let me go! Mom!</i>

50
00:02:20,849 --> 00:02:23,601
[goons hollering]

51
00:02:26,271 --> 00:02:28,231
[goons speaking indistinctly]

52
00:02:29,440 --> 00:02:31,317
[suspenseful music playing]

53
00:02:31,734 --> 00:02:33,570
[action music playing]

54
00:02:33,903 --> 00:02:34,988
[goon exclaims]

55
00:02:36,406 --> 00:02:37,407
[Diego] Hey!

56
00:02:41,995 --> 00:02:42,996
[grunts]

57
00:02:46,082 --> 00:02:48,126
[goon grunts and groans]

58
00:03:14,652 --> 00:03:16,779
[action music continues playing]

59
00:03:16,863 --> 00:03:17,864
[goon] Get up!

60
00:03:19,490 --> 00:03:20,491
[Diego grunts]

61
00:03:30,710 --> 00:03:31,711
[Ivy] Diego!

62
00:03:34,964 --> 00:03:35,965
[Ivy grunts]

63
00:03:41,763 --> 00:03:42,847
Diego!

64
00:04:05,787 --> 00:04:07,664
[goons grunting]

65
00:04:13,461 --> 00:04:14,462
[grunts]

66
00:04:30,853 --> 00:04:32,313
This is odd.

67
00:04:33,064 --> 00:04:37,068
Our gambling associates have
never been late to our meetings.

68
00:04:37,151 --> 00:04:40,863
I find it strange too.
Maybe they're just busy?

69
00:04:41,322 --> 00:04:45,493
[scoffs] Busy? Whenever I call a meeting,

70
00:04:45,576 --> 00:04:48,079
they always drop whatever they're doing.

71
00:04:48,621 --> 00:04:51,124
I'm telling you, Arnaldo,
something's not right.

72
00:04:53,126 --> 00:04:55,003
-[Segovia] Congressman.
-Oh, Segovia.

73
00:04:55,878 --> 00:04:57,714
Where are our partners?

74
00:04:58,506 --> 00:05:03,720
They all left. Jaguar took over
most of our gambling operations.

75
00:05:05,263 --> 00:05:06,806
[Julio] Son of a--

76
00:05:07,682 --> 00:05:08,641
[exhales sharply]

77
00:05:09,726 --> 00:05:11,019
[exasperated sigh]

78
00:05:16,232 --> 00:05:17,859
[indistinct chatter]

79
00:05:17,942 --> 00:05:20,320
[goon] It's Mr. Jaguar! Mr. Jaguar!

80
00:05:20,403 --> 00:05:23,489
[goons] Mr. Jaguar!

81
00:05:23,573 --> 00:05:24,824
[goon] Mr. Jaguar!

82
00:05:28,286 --> 00:05:29,203
Listen up!

83
00:05:29,996 --> 00:05:31,497
In order to show his appreciation,

84
00:05:31,581 --> 00:05:34,000
the Jaguar prepared a surprise for you.

85
00:05:34,083 --> 00:05:36,836
[tense music playing]

86
00:06:12,747 --> 00:06:14,749
Who ordered you to attack me?

87
00:06:16,334 --> 00:06:18,211
Who ordered you to do this?!

88
00:06:18,294 --> 00:06:19,170
[gunshots]

89
00:06:22,090 --> 00:06:27,011
Answer me. Who do you work for?
You don't want to answer me?

90
00:06:27,095 --> 00:06:29,931
Even if you don't tell me
who's behind this,

91
00:06:30,014 --> 00:06:32,183
-I know you work for Emilia!
-[gunshots]

92
00:06:33,601 --> 00:06:35,061
You're all scum!

93
00:06:38,147 --> 00:06:42,151
If you try to follow me,
I will kill you. You understand?

94
00:06:44,654 --> 00:06:45,613
Ivy, let's go.

95
00:06:45,696 --> 00:06:47,323
-Tell Emilia…
-Let's go.

96
00:06:47,406 --> 00:06:49,283
I'm not afraid of her!

97
00:06:49,784 --> 00:06:51,369
-Tell her that!
-[gunshots]

98
00:06:55,790 --> 00:06:59,752
[sighs] Looks like I'm going
to have a restful sleep.

99
00:07:00,711 --> 00:07:04,340
Wow. Finally. I so deserve
a good night's sleep.

100
00:07:04,799 --> 00:07:06,217
Beauty rest.

101
00:07:06,300 --> 00:07:09,887
Good. I hope you don't get nightmares.

102
00:07:12,098 --> 00:07:13,099
Aunt Claire…

103
00:07:13,558 --> 00:07:15,768
Why are you raining on my parade?

104
00:07:16,686 --> 00:07:20,606
Emilia, you've done a number of
unspeakable things in the past,

105
00:07:20,690 --> 00:07:23,025
and I never said anything about it.

106
00:07:24,569 --> 00:07:27,405
But to have another woman raped…

107
00:07:28,197 --> 00:07:29,615
That's unacceptable.

108
00:07:30,116 --> 00:07:31,868
Auntie, when it comes to that woman,

109
00:07:31,951 --> 00:07:33,411
I don't care about morals.

110
00:07:33,494 --> 00:07:35,079
And that's what she wants anyway, right?

111
00:07:35,163 --> 00:07:40,585
For men to lust after her.
That's why I'm giving it to her.

112
00:07:40,668 --> 00:07:43,546
Besides, you know, every time
I see that woman,

113
00:07:43,629 --> 00:07:45,089
you know, she's like Camia.

114
00:07:45,173 --> 00:07:48,217
They love it when men go crazy over them.

115
00:07:48,301 --> 00:07:51,012
That's the reason my husband fell for her.

116
00:07:51,095 --> 00:07:56,017
It's a good thing
my sex appeal's stronger than

117
00:07:56,100 --> 00:07:59,770
Camia's, that's why Raul
and I are still together.

118
00:07:59,854 --> 00:08:03,399
Honestly, the problem with these women

119
00:08:03,483 --> 00:08:05,485
is they only rely on their looks.

120
00:08:06,611 --> 00:08:10,114
If they rely on their looks,
what about you?

121
00:08:12,241 --> 00:08:14,660
Seriously, Auntie? Are we okay?

122
00:08:14,744 --> 00:08:16,412
Do we have a problem or an issue?

123
00:08:17,663 --> 00:08:21,542
You better give me the correct
answer, or you'll be sorry.

124
00:08:22,293 --> 00:08:24,545
What were you saying again?

125
00:08:24,629 --> 00:08:27,715
[ominous music playing]

126
00:08:27,798 --> 00:08:28,883
Nothing.

127
00:08:29,634 --> 00:08:30,801
Great.

128
00:08:40,520 --> 00:08:42,980
Let's go, Ivy! Wear this.

129
00:08:47,693 --> 00:08:48,945
Ivy, hold tight.

130
00:08:52,615 --> 00:08:56,494
[melancholic music playing]

131
00:09:27,525 --> 00:09:30,361
[Arnaldo] I think we should take
that Jaguar down, Grandpa.

132
00:09:30,945 --> 00:09:34,323
That is what I really plan to do.

133
00:09:36,242 --> 00:09:39,495
I can't wait to see
that Jaguar cower like a kitten.

134
00:09:40,580 --> 00:09:41,789
[Julio laughs]

135
00:09:43,124 --> 00:09:45,042
-Excuse me, Papa.
-Yes, Raul?

136
00:09:45,459 --> 00:09:46,419
Uh… [grunts]

137
00:09:46,502 --> 00:09:49,171
I'm going to put this here.
Someone wants you to have it.

138
00:09:50,631 --> 00:09:54,051
Don't touch it, Arnaldo.

139
00:09:54,135 --> 00:09:58,180
Jaguar sent that. I can feel it.

140
00:09:58,931 --> 00:10:00,808
Papa, if you don't mind me asking…

141
00:10:01,642 --> 00:10:03,644
What is it about that Jaguar?

142
00:10:03,728 --> 00:10:06,230
Are you afraid of him or something?

143
00:10:08,274 --> 00:10:10,192
I'm not afraid of anything, Raul.

144
00:10:11,277 --> 00:10:14,238
Now, just to humor you…

145
00:10:15,114 --> 00:10:17,033
Let's do it, let's open it!

146
00:10:18,784 --> 00:10:22,413
Let's see what Jaguar sent us this time.

147
00:10:29,879 --> 00:10:30,963
Oh…

148
00:10:33,299 --> 00:10:35,635
-What is that? Dirt?
-[Julio laughs]

149
00:10:36,594 --> 00:10:40,222
It's supposed to be symbolic, Arnaldo.

150
00:10:40,306 --> 00:10:42,391
It's a symbol of…

151
00:10:44,894 --> 00:10:45,853
death.

152
00:10:48,272 --> 00:10:50,232
[Julio] Silly Jaguar!

153
00:10:52,026 --> 00:10:53,361
What is he trying to say?

154
00:10:53,444 --> 00:10:56,113
If he was here, I'd dump that at his feet.

155
00:10:56,697 --> 00:11:02,578
Just to show him that his scare
tactics aren't working at all.

156
00:11:04,914 --> 00:11:06,707
You know what this is, Arnaldo?

157
00:11:08,292 --> 00:11:10,127
This was done by a child!

158
00:11:10,211 --> 00:11:13,005
This is a childish display of bravado!

159
00:11:14,006 --> 00:11:17,093
This Jaguar guy should ask
his mother for some tips

160
00:11:17,176 --> 00:11:20,638
on how to fight like a man.

161
00:11:23,099 --> 00:11:26,602
Well, anyway… Let's go!

162
00:11:27,436 --> 00:11:33,859
[groans] I've had my share of
bad comedy for the night.

163
00:11:35,027 --> 00:11:36,278
By the way…

164
00:11:39,073 --> 00:11:41,659
-Good night, Jaguar!
-[Arnaldo chuckles]

165
00:11:43,494 --> 00:11:46,747
-Excuse me, Raul. Good night.
-Okay, Papa.

166
00:11:46,831 --> 00:11:48,457
What should I do with this?

167
00:11:49,250 --> 00:11:50,376
Uh…

168
00:11:51,168 --> 00:11:54,797
You can either return it to Jaguar
or look for him

169
00:11:54,880 --> 00:11:56,715
and stuff him in that bag.

170
00:11:57,383 --> 00:11:59,468
[Julio laughs]

171
00:12:09,186 --> 00:12:10,354
Hey.

172
00:12:10,438 --> 00:12:12,314
I thought you were having
dinner with Ivy, Mom?

173
00:12:13,023 --> 00:12:15,109
That's what I thought too!

174
00:12:15,192 --> 00:12:19,196
I kept calling your girlfriend--
Sorry, I mean your fiancée,

175
00:12:19,280 --> 00:12:21,157
but she hasn't been answering my calls.

176
00:12:21,782 --> 00:12:25,077
You know what? That woman's
nothing but a pretty face.

177
00:12:25,161 --> 00:12:27,121
She has no class at all!

178
00:12:27,204 --> 00:12:29,707
Okay, enough with the insults, Mom.

179
00:12:29,790 --> 00:12:31,625
First of all, I don't believe you.

180
00:12:31,709 --> 00:12:36,464
It's either something bad happened to her,
or worse, you're behind all this.

181
00:12:36,547 --> 00:12:37,590
Wow!

182
00:12:39,383 --> 00:12:41,469
Mamita, tell me.

183
00:12:43,429 --> 00:12:44,805
Did Mom have something to do with this?

184
00:12:49,226 --> 00:12:50,186
No comment.

185
00:12:50,269 --> 00:12:51,437
[Julio scoffs]

186
00:12:51,520 --> 00:12:54,315
My grandson is asking a question.

187
00:12:55,941 --> 00:12:57,985
Where is Ivy Aguas?

188
00:12:58,068 --> 00:13:01,614
-Papa!
-I am not asking you.

189
00:13:01,697 --> 00:13:02,740
[sighs]

190
00:13:04,116 --> 00:13:06,577
I'm asking you though, Claire.

191
00:13:06,660 --> 00:13:09,997
[tense music playing]

192
00:13:14,001 --> 00:13:15,169
[Julio] Well?

193
00:13:15,252 --> 00:13:18,422
Are we just going to stand around,

194
00:13:18,506 --> 00:13:20,716
or will you keep the ball rolling?

195
00:13:23,260 --> 00:13:26,222
[somber music playing]

196
00:13:30,601 --> 00:13:31,519
Ivy…

197
00:13:37,942 --> 00:13:39,068
Follow me, Ivy.

198
00:13:47,284 --> 00:13:50,829
Let's spend the night here.
It's not safe right now.

199
00:14:01,799 --> 00:14:03,133
[phone ringing]

200
00:14:04,969 --> 00:14:06,679
[phone ringing]

201
00:14:07,513 --> 00:14:08,597
<i>Hello, Ivy?</i>

202
00:14:09,557 --> 00:14:10,641
<i>Who are you?</i>

203
00:14:11,183 --> 00:14:13,561
<i>-Ivy?!</i>
<i>-Where's Emilia?</i>

204
00:14:26,198 --> 00:14:29,785
Julio, I may not be an Ardiente by blood,

205
00:14:29,869 --> 00:14:31,620
but I know my alliances.

206
00:14:31,704 --> 00:14:33,706
And I won't jeopardize that!

207
00:14:33,789 --> 00:14:36,667
-[Julio] Okay.
-[Claire] That being said…

208
00:14:41,297 --> 00:14:44,341
No, Emilia had nothing to do with this.

209
00:14:44,425 --> 00:14:46,969
See, I told you!

210
00:14:47,052 --> 00:14:49,513
We shouldn't even be talking
about this to begin with!

211
00:14:49,597 --> 00:14:53,601
I had nothing to do with this!
Aunt Claire just said so!

212
00:14:54,268 --> 00:14:56,770
I'm really offended! For all we know,

213
00:14:56,854 --> 00:15:02,902
your girlfriend-slash-fiancée
went to see another man.

214
00:15:02,985 --> 00:15:06,822
Or maybe, she's hiding something.

215
00:15:08,782 --> 00:15:10,618
Auntie, let's go.

216
00:15:12,077 --> 00:15:13,245
[sighs] Good grief.

217
00:15:17,583 --> 00:15:21,879
How does that rhyme go? Liar, liar…

218
00:15:23,213 --> 00:15:24,506
Pants on fire.

219
00:15:24,840 --> 00:15:27,551
-[chuckles] That's your mom!
-[exhales heavily]

220
00:15:28,302 --> 00:15:30,721
[instrumental theme music playing]

221
00:15:36,310 --> 00:15:38,145
We'll make the Ardientes pay.

222
00:16:13,514 --> 00:16:15,182
[crying]

223
00:16:36,412 --> 00:16:38,122
I'm so sick of it.

224
00:16:40,916 --> 00:16:42,793
I want to give up.

225
00:16:43,502 --> 00:16:45,212
But if I do…

226
00:16:47,339 --> 00:16:48,716
I'll get killed.

227
00:16:52,344 --> 00:16:56,181
And I can't let the Ardientes
get away with the things they do.

228
00:16:57,224 --> 00:17:00,978
So, no matter how hard it is for me…

229
00:17:04,231 --> 00:17:08,152
even though it hurts so much,

230
00:17:08,235 --> 00:17:10,195
I have to endure

231
00:17:11,697 --> 00:17:14,033
because I have to keep fighting.

232
00:17:14,950 --> 00:17:19,788
I know that someday
it will all make sense.

233
00:17:24,043 --> 00:17:28,547
I won't let another child
or family experience

234
00:17:28,630 --> 00:17:30,716
what I had to go through.

235
00:17:32,092 --> 00:17:34,136
I won't let that happen.

236
00:17:37,222 --> 00:17:39,808
I won't let what happened
to Nanny Carlotta

237
00:17:39,892 --> 00:17:41,769
happen to anyone else.

238
00:17:44,229 --> 00:17:45,814
I won't let it.

239
00:17:45,898 --> 00:17:48,692
[instrumental theme music playing]

240
00:17:52,613 --> 00:17:54,156
And when you finally get justice…

241
00:17:56,617 --> 00:17:57,576
what will you do?

242
00:17:58,577 --> 00:18:00,746
I hope I do get it.

243
00:18:04,500 --> 00:18:08,378
When I do, I don't know.

244
00:18:12,091 --> 00:18:13,342
I don't know.

245
00:18:29,233 --> 00:18:32,194
That's it? You're just
going to frown at me?

246
00:18:32,736 --> 00:18:34,988
The least you can do is thank me.

247
00:18:35,405 --> 00:18:37,825
-For what?
-For keeping your secrets!

248
00:18:38,367 --> 00:18:42,538
Exhibit A. Hiring someone to spy on Diego.

249
00:18:42,621 --> 00:18:46,250
Exhibit B. What you did to Ivy.

250
00:18:46,708 --> 00:18:49,628
How much do you want
for keeping those secrets?

251
00:18:49,711 --> 00:18:50,838
[scoffs]

252
00:18:50,921 --> 00:18:54,216
You can't bribe me
with something you don't have.

253
00:18:56,051 --> 00:18:58,720
[crutches clacking]

254
00:19:03,016 --> 00:19:05,310
Bravo. Bravo.

255
00:19:07,062 --> 00:19:08,355
Bravo, Claire.

256
00:19:09,606 --> 00:19:16,238
Maybe we can offer you something
that we Ardientes do have.

257
00:19:17,197 --> 00:19:22,494
And that is… the protection
that we can provide you.

258
00:19:23,579 --> 00:19:26,248
Well, it's just an offer. Think about it.

259
00:19:26,623 --> 00:19:30,627
If you turn your back on us,
you're courting danger.

260
00:19:34,840 --> 00:19:36,008
[Julio] Hmm?

261
00:19:36,091 --> 00:19:39,303
-I'm not betraying you.
-Good, very good.

262
00:19:40,137 --> 00:19:41,180
Claire.

263
00:19:42,973 --> 00:19:45,017
Keep your secrets to yourself.

264
00:19:46,476 --> 00:19:51,815
And Emilia, my dear daughter,
I applaud you.

265
00:19:52,858 --> 00:19:55,194
I applaud your initiative.

266
00:19:56,153 --> 00:19:59,615
Finally, you learned something from me.

267
00:19:59,698 --> 00:20:03,785
Now, you're truly starting
to think like a true Ardiente.

268
00:20:04,578 --> 00:20:08,874
Placing a mole in Diego's camp.

269
00:20:11,460 --> 00:20:13,045
Stroke of brilliance.

270
00:20:13,879 --> 00:20:17,049
And the attack on Miss Aguas?

271
00:20:18,508 --> 00:20:21,094
Right target, good intention.

272
00:20:22,304 --> 00:20:23,472
Bad execution.

273
00:20:23,889 --> 00:20:25,891
-But, Papa?
-[Julio] Emilia.

274
00:20:25,974 --> 00:20:30,604
Don't treat Miss Aguas
like Raul's mistresses

275
00:20:30,687 --> 00:20:33,023
that you can easily get rid of.

276
00:20:33,690 --> 00:20:36,735
If Arnaldo finds out about what you did…

277
00:20:37,694 --> 00:20:38,987
[tut-tuts]

278
00:20:39,780 --> 00:20:42,407
Your son won't be able to forgive you.

279
00:20:42,491 --> 00:20:44,785
[tense music playing]

280
00:20:45,702 --> 00:20:47,955
A little advice to both of you, ladies.

281
00:20:50,207 --> 00:20:51,250
Carry on.

282
00:20:52,709 --> 00:20:55,587
But do tread lightly, ladies.

283
00:21:02,094 --> 00:21:04,429
Is there another appointment
you haven't told me about?

284
00:21:04,513 --> 00:21:06,014
Remember that I'm paying you

285
00:21:06,098 --> 00:21:08,725
to tell me any kind of
information about Miss Aguas.

286
00:21:08,809 --> 00:21:11,520
So, please, give me something!

287
00:21:11,603 --> 00:21:13,855
But there's nothing else, Mayor.

288
00:21:13,939 --> 00:21:14,815
Nothing?!

289
00:21:14,898 --> 00:21:16,275
-I'm sorry.
-Nothing?! You're useless!

290
00:21:16,358 --> 00:21:17,526
What do I pay you for?!

291
00:21:21,196 --> 00:21:23,282
When we finally get justice…

292
00:21:26,827 --> 00:21:28,412
I'll build a house here.

293
00:21:30,289 --> 00:21:34,418
I saved up for this,
because when I was a kid…

294
00:21:36,628 --> 00:21:38,463
I dreamed of having my own property.

295
00:21:41,008 --> 00:21:42,634
And I told myself…

296
00:21:45,304 --> 00:21:47,347
that I'd live here with…

297
00:21:49,474 --> 00:21:50,475
If…

298
00:21:51,143 --> 00:21:52,185
if she wants to…

299
00:21:54,229 --> 00:21:55,439
I'd live here with Lily.

300
00:21:57,399 --> 00:21:59,693
I know she'd love it here

301
00:21:59,776 --> 00:22:01,695
because it's far from the Ardientes.

302
00:22:07,409 --> 00:22:11,747
["Hindi Kita Iiwan" playing]

303
00:22:19,588 --> 00:22:22,174
Ivy, I want you to be happy.

304
00:22:24,801 --> 00:22:28,221
I want you to be free from this burden.

305
00:22:32,434 --> 00:22:34,519
I want you to be happy, Ivy.

306
00:22:36,855 --> 00:22:39,941
And I hope you'll let me be part of it.

307
00:22:49,701 --> 00:22:52,996
["Hindi Kita Iiwan" playing]

308
00:23:22,859 --> 00:23:23,860
Ivy.

309
00:23:27,656 --> 00:23:29,741
You know how much I love you, right?

310
00:23:50,595 --> 00:23:55,016
["Hindi Kita Iiwan" playing]

311
00:24:44,691 --> 00:24:46,651
[line ringing]

312
00:24:46,735 --> 00:24:47,986
Come on. Come on. Come on.

313
00:24:48,069 --> 00:24:49,654
-[line ringing]
-[screams]

314
00:24:50,405 --> 00:24:51,781
Answer the phone!

315
00:24:52,324 --> 00:24:54,576
[line ringing]

316
00:24:55,327 --> 00:24:56,661
-[line ringing]
-Ivy--

317
00:24:56,745 --> 00:24:57,787
[screams]

318
00:25:08,924 --> 00:25:12,636
[romantic music playing]

319
00:25:31,446 --> 00:25:33,240
Diego, I love you.

320
00:26:11,111 --> 00:26:13,530
I might find it hard to accept
most of your decisions.

321
00:26:16,032 --> 00:26:17,993
[Diego] <i>And I'm always worried about you.</i>

322
00:26:20,287 --> 00:26:21,788
<i>But there's one thing I'm sure of…</i>

323
00:26:23,081 --> 00:26:24,291
<i>You have a forgiving heart…</i>

324
00:26:27,335 --> 00:26:29,087
<i>and you remain to be a good person</i>

325
00:26:29,170 --> 00:26:31,715
<i>despite all the bad things</i>
<i>that happened to you.</i>

326
00:26:34,301 --> 00:26:36,052
Ivy, I promise you…

327
00:26:37,804 --> 00:26:39,931
that I'll be here for you until the end.

328
00:26:43,560 --> 00:26:47,105
I will do everything I can
to end your suffering.

329
00:26:53,069 --> 00:26:54,571
I love you so much.

330
00:26:54,654 --> 00:26:57,615
["Hindi Kita Iiwan" playing]

331
00:27:23,099 --> 00:27:25,101
I had Aunt Camia double-check everything.

332
00:27:25,685 --> 00:27:27,103
I'm prepared for my speech too.

333
00:27:27,604 --> 00:27:29,439
What about our program?

334
00:27:29,522 --> 00:27:32,901
It's all set. The band said
they'll perform for free too.

335
00:27:32,984 --> 00:27:34,486
<i>The sound system provider…</i>

336
00:27:34,569 --> 00:27:35,987
allowed us to pay them later.

337
00:27:36,071 --> 00:27:39,407
But let's make sure
to settle our balance on time.

338
00:27:40,367 --> 00:27:42,160
All right, I'll find a way.

339
00:27:42,494 --> 00:27:44,162
I'm actually here at my property.

340
00:27:44,704 --> 00:27:47,123
I'm planning on selling this
to get more funds.

341
00:27:47,624 --> 00:27:48,500
[Marlon] <i>Okay, good.</i>

342
00:27:48,583 --> 00:27:51,336
I'm sure a lot of people
would be interested in that.

343
00:27:51,419 --> 00:27:53,296
We can get more funds through that.

344
00:27:54,089 --> 00:27:55,840
Wait, where is that?
Do you want me to go there?

345
00:27:56,508 --> 00:27:57,634
No, don't. It's all right, Batch.

346
00:27:59,177 --> 00:27:59,928
<i>You always keep…</i>

347
00:28:00,011 --> 00:28:01,346
secrets from me.

348
00:28:02,764 --> 00:28:05,892
Wait. I think our future
governor got a girl.

349
00:28:05,975 --> 00:28:07,644
[Marlon laughs]

350
00:28:07,727 --> 00:28:10,021
So, tell me, who's the lucky woman?

351
00:28:11,106 --> 00:28:13,483
<i>Don't tell me you forgot about Lily.</i>

352
00:28:14,401 --> 00:28:16,861
You're nuts. Anyway, I have to go.

353
00:28:16,945 --> 00:28:18,530
[chuckles] All right. Okay.

354
00:28:20,865 --> 00:28:21,866
Diego.

355
00:28:23,243 --> 00:28:24,452
Thank you again…

356
00:28:26,037 --> 00:28:27,664
for what you did.

357
00:28:29,416 --> 00:28:30,458
Um…

358
00:28:32,085 --> 00:28:33,420
I need to go home.

359
00:28:34,003 --> 00:28:36,714
After that, I need to return
to the Ardiente's mansion

360
00:28:36,798 --> 00:28:40,385
because I can't just ignore
what Emilia did to me.

361
00:28:41,594 --> 00:28:43,012
Ivy, be careful.

362
00:28:44,222 --> 00:28:45,306
Uh…

363
00:28:47,183 --> 00:28:49,144
I didn't mean to eavesdrop…

364
00:28:49,227 --> 00:28:51,104
but are you really going
to sell this property?

365
00:28:53,273 --> 00:28:55,442
Diego, I know this is important to you.

366
00:28:56,943 --> 00:29:00,029
If it's okay with you,
I'd like to buy this property.

367
00:29:00,113 --> 00:29:06,119
So, when the time comes
that you need the land back,

368
00:29:06,202 --> 00:29:07,579
I'll give it.

369
00:29:08,580 --> 00:29:09,956
Ivy, I can't accept your offer.

370
00:29:11,249 --> 00:29:12,834
Thanks for your concern…

371
00:29:14,586 --> 00:29:18,298
but I want to win because of my hard work.

372
00:29:21,885 --> 00:29:26,139
But I promise that
I'll get this land back someday.

373
00:29:28,475 --> 00:29:29,559
Shall we go?

374
00:29:38,151 --> 00:29:40,820
What do you think about having
a motorcade before the filing?

375
00:29:40,904 --> 00:29:42,197
That's a good idea, Governor. We'll do it.

376
00:29:42,280 --> 00:29:43,072
Great, Jun.

377
00:29:43,156 --> 00:29:44,699
-Execute the plan.
-Let's take note of that.

378
00:29:44,783 --> 00:29:46,409
Let's execute that. Get it ready, okay?

379
00:29:47,619 --> 00:29:50,914
Arnaldo? Do you know
that I have better things to do

380
00:29:50,997 --> 00:29:55,126
than to watch you lose your head
like a lovesick puppy?

381
00:29:56,002 --> 00:29:57,045
[sighs]

382
00:29:57,462 --> 00:30:00,256
Your staff is here to give you
a briefing for tomorrow.

383
00:30:01,090 --> 00:30:03,426
As what Ma'am Emilia learned
from her intel,

384
00:30:03,510 --> 00:30:05,303
the opposition is ready.

385
00:30:05,386 --> 00:30:08,014
We won't back down.
We'll double our efforts.

386
00:30:08,097 --> 00:30:09,641
The cultural dancers
have already rehearsed.

387
00:30:09,724 --> 00:30:11,851
Aren't cultural dancers
a bit old-fashioned?

388
00:30:11,935 --> 00:30:14,562
We also have sexy dancers
to attract people.

389
00:30:14,646 --> 00:30:16,314
We'll be there first thing in the morning,

390
00:30:16,397 --> 00:30:18,233
to make them seem like the copycats.

391
00:30:18,316 --> 00:30:19,234
Right.

392
00:30:19,317 --> 00:30:22,153
Before we plan this, may I look
for my future first lady?

393
00:30:22,695 --> 00:30:23,988
Um…

394
00:30:24,072 --> 00:30:25,365
Guys, can you just leave us

395
00:30:25,448 --> 00:30:26,574
-for a while?
-Okay, Governor.

396
00:30:26,658 --> 00:30:27,951
-We'll just discuss things.
-Okay.

397
00:30:28,034 --> 00:30:29,828
-[groans]
-Thank you.

398
00:30:31,037 --> 00:30:31,871
[clears throat]

399
00:30:36,292 --> 00:30:38,253
-[Loring] Is this it?
-[Marlon] It's nice. Thank you.

400
00:30:38,336 --> 00:30:39,671
You can go now.

401
00:30:39,754 --> 00:30:41,005
-[Camia] Thank you!
-[Nimfa] Oh, please do eat.

402
00:30:41,089 --> 00:30:44,884
-[Diego] Thanks, Nimfa.
-[Loring] Take this, Diego.

403
00:30:44,968 --> 00:30:46,135
This is our donation.

404
00:30:46,219 --> 00:30:49,347
It's from Pandoy and the other farmers.

405
00:30:49,430 --> 00:30:50,765
Nanny, you shouldn't have.

406
00:30:50,849 --> 00:30:53,643
Thanks, but you shouldn't have pitched in.

407
00:30:53,726 --> 00:30:56,771
Diego, what do you mean we didn't need to?

408
00:30:56,855 --> 00:31:00,775
Of course, we need
to make sure you'll win!

409
00:31:00,859 --> 00:31:03,027
We're ready to sacrifice anything.

410
00:31:03,611 --> 00:31:04,571
Thanks, Nanny.

411
00:31:04,654 --> 00:31:05,864
[Loring and Marlon chuckling]

412
00:31:05,947 --> 00:31:08,825
[man] Diego, we're thankful
for your compassion.

413
00:31:08,908 --> 00:31:11,536
Especially when you fought
to protect our land

414
00:31:11,619 --> 00:31:13,496
from being stolen by the Ardientes.

415
00:31:13,580 --> 00:31:17,166
That's why we'll do everything
to help you win, right?

416
00:31:17,250 --> 00:31:18,918
[everyone agrees]

417
00:31:19,002 --> 00:31:20,587
-Thank you so much!
-Right. Right.

418
00:31:20,670 --> 00:31:22,213
-That's right.
-Thank you.

419
00:31:22,297 --> 00:31:23,131
[Loring] Yeah.

420
00:31:23,214 --> 00:31:26,509
We assure you that once Diego
has liquidated his property,

421
00:31:26,593 --> 00:31:28,511
and has been taken in by a party,

422
00:31:28,595 --> 00:31:30,847
we're going to give you your money back.

423
00:31:30,930 --> 00:31:34,934
But, Sir Marlon, which party
will Diego be running with?

424
00:31:35,518 --> 00:31:39,522
I hope it's a huge party, so the
Ardientes won't stand a chance!

425
00:31:39,898 --> 00:31:41,149
That's right.

426
00:31:41,232 --> 00:31:44,277
Nimfa, what about your father, Fernan?

427
00:31:44,360 --> 00:31:45,862
Is he joining the rally tomorrow?

428
00:31:45,945 --> 00:31:48,114
I haven't seen him around. Where is he?

429
00:31:48,197 --> 00:31:49,616
-[Pandoy] Yeah, that's right.
-[man] Yeah.

430
00:31:49,699 --> 00:31:51,743
-[Marlon] He's gone?
-[Loring] Yeah?

431
00:31:52,076 --> 00:31:56,331
Um, he's in Manila right now,
taking care of some business.

432
00:31:56,414 --> 00:31:58,124
He didn't want to leave,

433
00:31:58,207 --> 00:32:01,127
because he wants to help
with Diego's campaign.

434
00:32:01,210 --> 00:32:04,422
But it's okay because we'll get
back at those corrupt

435
00:32:04,505 --> 00:32:07,300
and heartless Ardientes!

436
00:32:07,383 --> 00:32:09,552
[loudly] I can't understand
why they keep winning!

437
00:32:09,636 --> 00:32:12,138
That's why we should unite
for Diego's cause!

438
00:32:12,221 --> 00:32:13,556
[everyone agrees]

439
00:32:13,640 --> 00:32:15,683
[indistinct chatter]

440
00:32:15,767 --> 00:32:17,435
[Nimfa] I'm sorry.

441
00:32:17,518 --> 00:32:20,146
I'm really sorry. I'm so sorry.

442
00:32:20,229 --> 00:32:23,358
When I talk about the Ardientes,
I get so worked up.

443
00:32:23,441 --> 00:32:25,276
[everyone laughs]

444
00:32:25,360 --> 00:32:26,444
[Pandoy] Same here!

445
00:32:26,527 --> 00:32:27,779
[Loring] You're just like your father!

446
00:32:27,862 --> 00:32:30,031
[Marlon] I guess so, right?

447
00:32:32,450 --> 00:32:37,413
Arnaldo, you're the governor,
not that woman. She's useless!

448
00:32:37,497 --> 00:32:41,417
I won't file for that
damn candidacy until I find Ivy.

449
00:32:41,501 --> 00:32:42,919
Okay? That's final.

450
00:32:43,002 --> 00:32:45,546
No. It is not final, Arnaldo.

451
00:32:46,422 --> 00:32:49,550
Look at you. What's happening
to you? What's wrong?

452
00:32:50,009 --> 00:32:52,178
You know, that woman's
trying to brainwash you.

453
00:32:52,261 --> 00:32:55,390
Now, you're even going
against your own mother!

454
00:32:55,765 --> 00:32:58,017
You keep taking her side over mine.

455
00:32:58,101 --> 00:33:01,312
Your own flesh and blood.
How can you do this, Arnaldo?!

456
00:33:01,771 --> 00:33:04,691
You're even jeopardizing
your own political career

457
00:33:04,774 --> 00:33:06,317
for that woman!

458
00:33:06,401 --> 00:33:08,987
And I'm not gonna allow this
to happen, Arnaldo.

459
00:33:09,070 --> 00:33:09,946
I'm not!

460
00:33:10,029 --> 00:33:12,949
[scoffs] Thing is, Ivy isn't the problem.

461
00:33:13,324 --> 00:33:14,325
You are!

462
00:33:15,326 --> 00:33:19,205
You can't accept that I'm marrying her.
I don't get it! What's your problem?

463
00:33:19,288 --> 00:33:24,127
You know why?
Because I despise that woman.

464
00:33:24,877 --> 00:33:28,214
You know, I'm like a mad dog
dying to shred her into pieces

465
00:33:28,297 --> 00:33:29,716
every time I see her!

466
00:33:30,216 --> 00:33:33,886
Until all that's left of her
are her rotting skin and bones.

467
00:33:33,970 --> 00:33:36,556
And I just happen to be your mother,

468
00:33:36,639 --> 00:33:38,307
and I'll do everything in my power

469
00:33:38,391 --> 00:33:41,102
to call off your wedding to that woman!

470
00:33:41,853 --> 00:33:44,355
Even if it takes having her killed!

471
00:33:44,439 --> 00:33:45,606
How dare you!

472
00:33:46,691 --> 00:33:47,608
I'm on the verge of forgetting

473
00:33:47,692 --> 00:33:50,361
that you're my mother and
slapping your beautiful face!

474
00:33:50,445 --> 00:33:52,697
The moment something happens
to Ivy, you will answer to me!

475
00:33:52,780 --> 00:33:53,865
Remember that.

476
00:33:56,159 --> 00:33:57,285
Remember that.

477
00:33:57,994 --> 00:34:00,038
You're insane. You're sick!

478
00:34:09,297 --> 00:34:11,632
Excuse me. There's a letter for Mr…

479
00:34:11,716 --> 00:34:12,759
-Diego Torillo.
-Batch…

480
00:34:12,842 --> 00:34:13,634
go get some snacks.

481
00:34:13,718 --> 00:34:15,303
[man] Diego, someone's looking for you!

482
00:34:15,386 --> 00:34:16,804
-Hey, Diego.
-[man] You have mail.

483
00:34:16,888 --> 00:34:17,805
[Loring] What?

484
00:34:18,389 --> 00:34:19,182
What is it?

485
00:34:19,265 --> 00:34:20,725
-There's a letter for you.
-It's a letter.

486
00:34:20,808 --> 00:34:23,394
-Delivery.
-I'm Diego.

487
00:34:23,478 --> 00:34:24,812
Kindly sign here, sir.

488
00:34:28,066 --> 00:34:30,068
Here you go. Thank you.

489
00:34:30,151 --> 00:34:31,569
Thank you, sir.

490
00:34:33,154 --> 00:34:34,405
-[Loring] Oh.
-Take care.

491
00:34:34,489 --> 00:34:35,907
[indistinct chatter]

492
00:34:37,200 --> 00:34:38,034
What's in it?

493
00:34:38,117 --> 00:34:40,328
-Hey, that's a check.
-A check?

494
00:34:40,411 --> 00:34:41,204
That's a check?

495
00:34:41,287 --> 00:34:42,538
-What is this?
-Nanny…

496
00:34:43,664 --> 00:34:44,707
[Pandoy] Whoa!

497
00:34:45,208 --> 00:34:48,753
[both blabbering]

498
00:34:48,836 --> 00:34:49,712
[man] That's a huge amount.

499
00:34:49,796 --> 00:34:51,923
-[Marlon] That's big.
-[Camia] Who sent this?

500
00:34:52,006 --> 00:34:54,008
Miss Camia, it's from an anonymous donor.

501
00:34:54,092 --> 00:34:57,261
This will be a great help to our campaign,

502
00:34:57,345 --> 00:34:59,222
and we can build
our headquarters with this.

503
00:34:59,305 --> 00:35:01,182
-Exactly!
-Right?

504
00:35:01,265 --> 00:35:02,683
[indistinct chatter]

505
00:35:02,767 --> 00:35:03,810
[Loring] What should we do?

506
00:35:03,893 --> 00:35:06,395
We better keep it somewhere safe.

507
00:35:06,479 --> 00:35:10,316
Nanny, hold on.
We can't just accept this money.

508
00:35:10,900 --> 00:35:13,778
Who would donate this much money?

509
00:35:13,861 --> 00:35:16,572
Batch, candidates always
receive anonymous donations.

510
00:35:16,656 --> 00:35:20,159
These donors try to help
the candidates they want to win.

511
00:35:20,243 --> 00:35:21,786
The candidates they believe in.

512
00:35:21,869 --> 00:35:24,413
And these donors are big-time businessmen.

513
00:35:24,497 --> 00:35:25,289
[Loring] My goodness.

514
00:35:25,373 --> 00:35:29,377
I'm sure this person has an ax
to grind with the Ardientes.

515
00:35:29,460 --> 00:35:31,295
-[laughter]
-[indistinct chatter]

516
00:35:31,963 --> 00:35:32,713
[Pandoy] That's right!

517
00:35:32,797 --> 00:35:34,090
[Marlon] We're on the same side.

518
00:35:34,715 --> 00:35:37,844
Diego, take it.

519
00:35:38,719 --> 00:35:42,557
That's for your campaign
and for our whole cause!

520
00:35:42,640 --> 00:35:43,641
Right, everyone?

521
00:35:43,724 --> 00:35:48,938
-[everyone agrees]
-[indistinct chatter]

522
00:35:53,693 --> 00:35:56,279
[singing and humming]

523
00:35:56,863 --> 00:35:57,905
Emilia!

524
00:35:57,989 --> 00:35:59,949
[suspenseful music playing]

525
00:36:05,580 --> 00:36:06,789
I-- Ivy…

526
00:36:12,378 --> 00:36:14,046
[stammers] What are you doing here?

527
00:36:16,299 --> 00:36:17,842
What am I doing here?

528
00:36:21,679 --> 00:36:25,933
I'm here to show you that
I am very much alive and well.

529
00:36:26,726 --> 00:36:28,394
Of course, you are, you should be.

530
00:36:29,604 --> 00:36:31,272
[grunts]

531
00:36:32,857 --> 00:36:37,153
-[smashes piano]
-[Emilia coughing]

532
00:36:38,070 --> 00:36:40,573
You bitch! Stop playing dumb

533
00:36:40,656 --> 00:36:45,286
because I know you're the one
who hired those men to rape me!

534
00:36:45,369 --> 00:36:50,458
I'm here to tell you
that you can never take me down.

535
00:36:50,541 --> 00:36:51,334
[smashes piano]

536
00:36:51,417 --> 00:36:54,003
What? Cat got your tongue?

537
00:36:55,213 --> 00:36:56,130
What?

538
00:37:00,468 --> 00:37:02,970
What is it, Emilia? Go on.

539
00:37:03,054 --> 00:37:07,266
You were saying? What do you want to say?

540
00:37:07,808 --> 00:37:09,518
Why are you blaming me?

541
00:37:09,602 --> 00:37:11,103
Why not?!

542
00:37:11,187 --> 00:37:13,439
I'm not playing games with you!

543
00:37:13,522 --> 00:37:14,607
[Emilia grunts]

544
00:37:16,234 --> 00:37:17,985
Remember this, Emilia.

545
00:37:18,069 --> 00:37:20,321
Remember this. Remember this!

546
00:37:21,072 --> 00:37:24,200
That's the last time you'll ever
get a chance to finish me off.

547
00:37:24,283 --> 00:37:29,997
Because next time,
I won't hesitate to kill you.

548
00:37:30,081 --> 00:37:37,046
I'll kill you! I will kill you! You bitch!

549
00:37:37,129 --> 00:37:40,216
[tense music playing]

550
00:37:43,928 --> 00:37:44,929
FOR THE NEW ARDIENTE

551
00:37:45,972 --> 00:37:48,516
Batch, this looks great! Right, Uncle?

552
00:37:48,599 --> 00:37:49,642
And these too.

553
00:37:49,725 --> 00:37:52,770
We'll make more of those
and give them to your supporters.

554
00:37:52,853 --> 00:37:57,525
-Diego, add this to the fund.
-Thank you, Auntie.

555
00:37:57,608 --> 00:37:58,526
[Pandoy] Wow.

556
00:37:58,609 --> 00:38:00,695
[Loring] I'm getting worried about this.

557
00:38:00,778 --> 00:38:04,031
Do we really have to place
the funds here in the house?

558
00:38:05,116 --> 00:38:08,411
Here, I made some coffee and snacks.

559
00:38:08,494 --> 00:38:09,370
Thank you, Nimfa.

560
00:38:09,453 --> 00:38:10,496
-Thanks.
-[Loring] Thanks.

561
00:38:10,579 --> 00:38:11,664
[Diego] Thank you.

562
00:38:11,747 --> 00:38:15,126
Nanny, you're the one I trust the most.

563
00:38:15,793 --> 00:38:17,628
Besides, we'd all feel safer

564
00:38:17,712 --> 00:38:20,256
if all the campaign materials
were kept here.

565
00:38:21,799 --> 00:38:26,846
All right. Okay. Here then.
I better put this away.

566
00:38:26,929 --> 00:38:28,264
[Pandoy] All right. We better put it away.

567
00:38:28,347 --> 00:38:29,223
[Loring] Yeah. That's right.

568
00:38:29,307 --> 00:38:36,063
We better take these too
and post them all over town.

569
00:38:36,147 --> 00:38:38,774
We better go too. Batch.
Let's go, Kris. Let's go.

570
00:38:38,858 --> 00:38:40,067
-Let's go.
-Bye, Miss. Camia.

571
00:38:40,151 --> 00:38:42,194
-Take care.
-Let's go. Let's go.

572
00:38:42,278 --> 00:38:43,863
-See you later, Batch.
-I'll come back for it later.

573
00:38:43,946 --> 00:38:45,531
-All right.
-[Pandoy] Loring!

574
00:38:45,614 --> 00:38:47,700
-[Loring] Yes?
-[Pandoy] Come with us.

575
00:38:47,783 --> 00:38:49,827
[Pandoy] We're going to
distribute these to the voters.

576
00:38:51,620 --> 00:38:54,540
-Let's go, Mrs. Loring.
-Okay.

577
00:38:55,708 --> 00:38:58,836
-Take care, guys.
-[Loring] We will. Thanks.

578
00:39:03,007 --> 00:39:04,091
Aunt Camia.

579
00:39:05,384 --> 00:39:07,053
I need to tell you something.

580
00:39:08,804 --> 00:39:10,306
Have you spoken to Ivy?

581
00:39:12,391 --> 00:39:13,225
[smashes piano]

582
00:39:13,309 --> 00:39:16,771
-You want that, huh?!
-[Emilia groaning]

583
00:39:16,854 --> 00:39:19,398
-Maybe it's time for you to die.
-Ivy? Mom!

584
00:39:19,482 --> 00:39:22,818
Ivy! Let go! Let go! Enough! Enough!

585
00:39:22,902 --> 00:39:24,612
-What the hell is wrong with you two?
-What happened?

586
00:39:24,695 --> 00:39:27,031
Do you know what your mother did?! Huh?!

587
00:39:28,491 --> 00:39:31,369
She sent her men to try and rape me!

588
00:39:31,452 --> 00:39:35,164
And I'm sure she planned to kill me too!

589
00:39:36,207 --> 00:39:37,208
Is it true?

590
00:39:39,251 --> 00:39:40,836
Answer me. Is it true?

591
00:39:43,005 --> 00:39:44,173
Well, Emilia?

592
00:39:46,175 --> 00:39:48,803
Say something.
Your son asked you a question!

593
00:39:50,388 --> 00:39:51,347
[Camia] What?!

594
00:39:51,430 --> 00:39:53,432
Emilia sent people to rape my daughter?

595
00:39:54,100 --> 00:39:57,103
Diego. I have to talk to her right now.

596
00:39:57,186 --> 00:39:59,855
I have to make sure
that my daughter is okay.

597
00:39:59,939 --> 00:40:03,317
Auntie, wait. Ivy's all right.
Don't worry.

598
00:40:03,859 --> 00:40:05,236
Were you the one who saved her?

599
00:40:07,780 --> 00:40:09,782
My poor daughter!

600
00:40:10,366 --> 00:40:12,910
When will her suffering end?

601
00:40:13,911 --> 00:40:16,539
Diego, I want to see her.

602
00:40:17,123 --> 00:40:19,041
I want to hug my daughter.

603
00:40:19,750 --> 00:40:21,710
And I want to face Emilia…

604
00:40:23,212 --> 00:40:26,966
so that I can beat her senseless.

605
00:40:27,049 --> 00:40:28,634
Aunt Camia, calm down.

606
00:40:30,094 --> 00:40:32,012
I know this isn't easy for you.

607
00:40:32,388 --> 00:40:34,140
But if you let your anger
get the best of you,

608
00:40:34,223 --> 00:40:36,517
it might ruin Ivy's plans.

609
00:40:37,393 --> 00:40:39,061
There's a right time to be angry.

610
00:40:39,979 --> 00:40:41,605
That's what I learned from Ivy.

611
00:40:42,773 --> 00:40:47,987
Right now, we should prepare for
our meeting with the Ardientes.

612
00:40:53,075 --> 00:40:55,035
[Julio] Excuse me, ladies.

613
00:40:56,078 --> 00:40:57,204
Emilia…

614
00:40:57,288 --> 00:41:01,459
Why do you think Miss Aguas
is accusing you of that?

615
00:41:02,209 --> 00:41:04,336
Papa, why would I do that?!

616
00:41:04,420 --> 00:41:08,507
Why would I even do that?
This woman is delusional!

617
00:41:08,591 --> 00:41:10,926
She's sick in the head. A major cuckoo!

618
00:41:11,010 --> 00:41:14,180
-Ivy, Ivy, Ivy.
-Delusional? Are you sure?

619
00:41:15,181 --> 00:41:17,600
You're the only one
who could've done that to me.

620
00:41:18,184 --> 00:41:20,769
-Do you have any proof?
-You want proof?

621
00:41:20,853 --> 00:41:22,521
Who made the reservation
at the restaurant?

622
00:41:22,605 --> 00:41:24,482
Wasn't it you? It was under your name.

623
00:41:24,565 --> 00:41:25,524
But where were you?

624
00:41:25,608 --> 00:41:28,194
I was trying to call you,
but you weren't picking up.

625
00:41:28,277 --> 00:41:30,112
-How's that?!
-I know it was you.

626
00:41:30,196 --> 00:41:32,615
You're the only one
who could have done that to me.

627
00:41:32,698 --> 00:41:33,616
You know what, Ivy?

628
00:41:33,699 --> 00:41:36,452
Since you're so good at making up stories,

629
00:41:36,535 --> 00:41:39,371
you should go see a doctor
because you're sick in the head!

630
00:41:39,455 --> 00:41:40,956
-Major cuckoo!
-I'm not sick in the head!

631
00:41:41,040 --> 00:41:43,209
-You're crazy!
-And I'm not making things up!

632
00:41:43,792 --> 00:41:46,086
You're such a good actress.

633
00:41:46,170 --> 00:41:49,298
Why don't you see a doctor, instead?

634
00:41:49,381 --> 00:41:51,550
Because no mother in her
right mind would ever send men

635
00:41:51,634 --> 00:41:54,428
to rape her future daughter-in-law.

636
00:41:57,556 --> 00:41:58,766
You're crazy.

637
00:42:09,068 --> 00:42:12,196
Be thankful I'm friends with the chief,

638
00:42:12,279 --> 00:42:14,782
or you'd all be in jail right now!

639
00:42:14,865 --> 00:42:19,828
Incompetent fools! You're all pathetic!

640
00:42:19,912 --> 00:42:22,540
How could all of you
let one woman get away?!

641
00:42:22,623 --> 00:42:25,042
[goon] She wasn't alone, ma'am.

642
00:42:25,876 --> 00:42:27,294
Diego was there to help her.

643
00:42:27,378 --> 00:42:30,422
I don't care! You're useless! [grunts]

644
00:42:31,924 --> 00:42:35,886
Nobody talks to anyone
about this! Is that clear?!

645
00:42:35,970 --> 00:42:38,764
-Yes, ma'am.
-Leave, now!

646
00:42:52,278 --> 00:42:54,029
[phone ringing]

647
00:42:56,699 --> 00:42:58,284
[phone ringing]

648
00:42:58,367 --> 00:43:00,369
[ominous music playing]

649
00:43:02,955 --> 00:43:03,956
[clears throat]

650
00:43:05,207 --> 00:43:08,210
-Hello, Nimfa.
-Hello, ma'am.

651
00:43:08,294 --> 00:43:12,089
Make sure that Diego and
his group don't find out

652
00:43:12,172 --> 00:43:14,675
I sent my men to rape Ivy, okay?

653
00:43:14,758 --> 00:43:15,843
Uh…

654
00:43:16,635 --> 00:43:17,886
Of course, Ma'am Emilia.

655
00:43:18,679 --> 00:43:20,264
<i>Oh, by the way…</i>

656
00:43:20,806 --> 00:43:23,934
I know where Camia's funds are hidden.

657
00:43:24,226 --> 00:43:26,770
<i>And it came from an anonymous donor.</i>

658
00:43:27,146 --> 00:43:29,607
<i>It seems like Diego</i>
<i>and his group are rich now.</i>

659
00:43:29,690 --> 00:43:32,610
That's rich enough for you? [chuckles]

660
00:43:32,693 --> 00:43:35,362
That's nothing compared
to what the Ardientes have.

661
00:43:37,031 --> 00:43:38,782
Okay, Ma'am Emilia…

662
00:43:39,199 --> 00:43:44,371
So, you take care of Ivy,
while I take care of Camia.

663
00:43:44,913 --> 00:43:46,206
<i>I can feel it too.</i>

664
00:43:46,290 --> 00:43:48,083
I'll catch those two together.

665
00:43:48,792 --> 00:43:55,674
Okay, just make sure you keep
your promise before I keep mine.

666
00:43:55,758 --> 00:43:58,761
[tense music playing]

667
00:44:11,857 --> 00:44:13,692
She will not get away with this!

668
00:44:13,776 --> 00:44:14,860
I'm telling you…

669
00:44:14,943 --> 00:44:18,155
Tell me what those men
looked like, and I swear,

670
00:44:18,238 --> 00:44:21,659
I'll kill them all!
I'll kill my mother too.

671
00:44:22,493 --> 00:44:24,703
I swear, I will do everything for you.

672
00:44:25,496 --> 00:44:26,789
I will avenge you…

673
00:44:27,498 --> 00:44:30,918
I will avenge you, and I'll make
sure everyone suffers.

674
00:44:31,627 --> 00:44:33,337
I'll make sure everyone suffers.

675
00:44:35,422 --> 00:44:36,965
Every single one of them.

676
00:44:40,469 --> 00:44:42,304
Leave me, Mr. Mayor.

677
00:44:45,724 --> 00:44:47,518
"Mr. Mayor"? I am your fiancé.

678
00:44:47,601 --> 00:44:49,520
I'm… I'm not going anywhere!

679
00:44:49,978 --> 00:44:51,897
Okay? I'm not going anywhere.
I'm staying here.

680
00:44:52,231 --> 00:44:54,149
I can take care of myself.

681
00:44:54,983 --> 00:44:58,529
Well, I used to have Nanny
Carlotta to take care of me,

682
00:44:58,612 --> 00:45:00,948
but now, she's gone.

683
00:45:01,698 --> 00:45:03,992
So, whoever killed her…

684
00:45:04,993 --> 00:45:08,622
should know that it feels like
I've died too.

685
00:45:09,373 --> 00:45:10,457
[sighs]

686
00:45:11,625 --> 00:45:12,751
Ivy…

687
00:45:14,711 --> 00:45:18,632
Carlotta is gone, but I am here, okay?

688
00:45:19,425 --> 00:45:22,678
I'm your family now,
so I'm not going anywhere.

689
00:45:24,388 --> 00:45:25,431
Okay?

690
00:45:27,850 --> 00:45:29,810
I'm not going anywhere. I'm here for you.

691
00:45:34,273 --> 00:45:36,942
[Diego] <i>Ivy, I want you to be happy.</i>

692
00:45:37,025 --> 00:45:40,612
<i>I want you to be free from this burden.</i>

693
00:45:40,696 --> 00:45:42,698
<i>I want you to be happy, Ivy.</i>

694
00:45:43,115 --> 00:45:45,868
<i>And I hope you'll let me be part of it.</i>

695
00:45:45,951 --> 00:45:49,163
<i>Ivy, you know how much I love you, right?</i>

696
00:45:49,830 --> 00:45:51,081
[Ivy] <i>Diego, I love you.</i>

697
00:45:57,546 --> 00:45:58,964
I'm not going anywhere.

698
00:46:01,842 --> 00:46:03,010
I'm staying right here.

699
00:46:15,481 --> 00:46:20,235
<i>I'll keep fighting until</i>
<i>we can be together, Ivy.</i>

700
00:46:26,658 --> 00:46:30,746
[screaming] <i>Who did this to you?!</i>

701
00:46:31,788 --> 00:46:35,167
<i>Tell me!</i>

702
00:46:36,251 --> 00:46:41,423
<i>A-A-T. Arnaldo Ardiente-Torillo.</i>

703
00:46:41,507 --> 00:46:45,802
<i>What do you have to do</i>
<i>with Nanny Carlotta's death?</i>

704
00:46:48,305 --> 00:46:50,432
[indistinct chatter]

705
00:46:54,186 --> 00:46:56,688
[Emilia] <i>Do you know</i>
<i>what your mother did?!</i>

706
00:46:56,772 --> 00:46:59,650
<i>She sent her men to try and rape me!</i>

707
00:46:59,733 --> 00:47:03,195
<i>And I'm sure she planned to kill me too!</i>

708
00:47:05,864 --> 00:47:07,449
[tense music playing]

709
00:47:07,533 --> 00:47:08,659
Get away from me.

710
00:47:10,369 --> 00:47:11,537
Hon, what's wrong?

711
00:47:12,913 --> 00:47:13,914
What's wrong?

712
00:47:14,581 --> 00:47:16,500
-Get away from me.
-What's wrong?! Hey!

713
00:47:16,583 --> 00:47:18,544
-Get away, Arnaldo!
-What's with you?!

714
00:47:20,921 --> 00:47:23,173
-Get away!
-[screams] Is it my fault?!

715
00:47:25,217 --> 00:47:26,343
Tell me!

716
00:47:29,304 --> 00:47:30,722
I don't get you.

717
00:47:31,723 --> 00:47:34,017
I'm trying my best to understand you.

718
00:47:34,851 --> 00:47:38,564
Okay, fine. Given… Given you're in shock.

719
00:47:41,525 --> 00:47:45,487
Fine. I will go the extra mile
to understand you.

720
00:47:45,946 --> 00:47:46,947
Fine.

721
00:47:48,448 --> 00:47:49,449
Get some rest.

722
00:47:51,368 --> 00:47:54,621
Rest for tonight, so you can come with me

723
00:47:54,705 --> 00:47:55,831
when I file for candidacy.

724
00:47:59,585 --> 00:48:02,421
I love you. I love you, Ivy.

725
00:48:06,550 --> 00:48:08,051
I love you so much.

726
00:48:08,594 --> 00:48:09,803
Arnaldo, please.

727
00:48:11,805 --> 00:48:13,015
Go home.

728
00:48:13,098 --> 00:48:15,601
[dramatic music playing]

729
00:48:41,335 --> 00:48:44,296
[tense music playing]

730
00:48:48,967 --> 00:48:52,012
[supporters] <i>Diego! Diego! Diego! Diego!</i>

731
00:48:52,095 --> 00:48:54,473
[Camia]<i> You are the queen of hired killers</i>

732
00:48:54,556 --> 00:48:56,725
<i>and hired rapists in this place!</i>

733
00:48:56,808 --> 00:49:00,312
<i>Why would you even think</i>
<i>that Ivy would be supporting us</i>

734
00:49:00,395 --> 00:49:02,522
<i>if she knew that I was the one</i>
<i>who tried to have her raped?</i>

735
00:49:02,606 --> 00:49:04,191
<i>Ivy, come on. Speak up.</i>

736
00:49:06,068 --> 00:49:08,278
[screaming]

737
00:49:08,362 --> 00:49:09,696
[Ivy] <i>What happened? Oh, my.</i>

738
00:49:09,780 --> 00:49:11,823
<i>Congressman, could this be an inside job?</i>

739
00:49:12,574 --> 00:49:16,119
[Emilia] <i>Sabotage.</i>
<i>I want to cripple them all.</i>

740
00:49:16,203 --> 00:49:18,121
[Nimfa] <i>You'll be surprised, ma'am.</i>

741
00:49:18,205 --> 00:49:20,582
<i>I can say that it'll be a blast.</i>

742
00:49:21,458 --> 00:49:24,211
[theme music playing]
